ef 1083 #uuid "7f2aabc6-1d15-561e-90e2-6684ee1deb5a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186549684 #edb/ref 1080 "An empty set" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186549684 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186549684 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "c5afc31f-1a53-53aa-b386-bc68f24950e9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186549772 #edb/ref 1080 "A pair of parallel lines" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186549772 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186549772 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "f58f9c99-39e6-5a04-b920-e4b11dd89485" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186549805 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186549359 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186549805 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186549511 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186549805 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186549553 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186549805 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186549684 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186549805 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186549772 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186549805 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186549805 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186549805 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186549553 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186549805 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "178efdfc-1a0b-5ff3-b766-30d0f0cf8760" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186550002 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186549805 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186550002 #edb/ref 1069 "q-140569" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186550002 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186550002 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the change of variables given by the matrix equation\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{5} & \\frac{4}{5} \\\\ \\frac{4}{5} & \\frac{3}{5}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nand the curve $C,$ defined as\n\n$$\nC:\\,9{x}_{1}^{2}-24{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+16{x}_{2}^{2}-50{x}_{1}+25{x}_{2}=0.\n$$\n\n \n\nGiven that the change of variables above reduces $Q(x)=9{x}_{1}^{2}-24{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+16{x}_{2}^{2}$ to its canonical (diagonal) form $25{y}_{1}^{2}$ what type of a quadratic curve is defined by $C?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186550002 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d27201ee-27d4-58dc-b2ff-368cd1c77509" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186550002 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we note the following:\n\n$$\nC:\\,{{9{x}_{1}^{2}-24{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+16{x}_{2}^{2}}_{⏟}}_{Q(x)}-50{x}_{1}+25{x}_{2}=0\n$$\n\nLet's write the given change of variables explicitly:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{5} & \\frac{4}{5} \\\\ \\frac{4}{5} & \\frac{3}{5}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}=\\frac{4}{5}{y}_{2}-\\frac{3}{5}{y}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}=\\frac{4}{5}{y}_{1}+\\frac{3}{5}{y}_{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe know that the given change of variables reduces $Q(x)$ to its canonical form. Therefore, performing the change of variables on $C,$ we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9{x}_{1}^{2}-24{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+16{x}_{2}^{2}-50{x}_{1}+25{x}_{2} & =0 \\\\ 25{y}_{1}^{2}-50(\\frac{4}{5}{y}_{2}-\\frac{3}{5}{y}_{1})+25(\\frac{4}{5}{y}_{1}+\\frac{3}{5}{y}_{2}) & =0 \\\\ 25{y}_{1}^{2}+50{y}_{1}-25{y}_{2} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we complete the square for the variable ${y}_{1}:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}25{y}_{1}^{2}+50{y}_{1}-25{y}_{2} & =0 \\\\ {y}_{1}^{2}+2{y}_{1}-{y}_{2} & =0 \\\\ {y}_{1}^{2}+2{y}_{1}+1-1-{y}_{2} & =0 \\\\ ({y}_{1}+1)^{2}-1-{y}_{2} & =0 \\\\ ({y}_{1}+1)^{2} & ={y}_{2}+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, performing the change of variables \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{z}_{1}={y}_{1}+1, \\\\ {z}_{2}={y}_{2}+1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({y}_{1}+1)^{2} & ={y}_{2}+1 \\\\ {z}_{1}^{2} & ={z}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThis represents a parabola that opens in the direction of the positive ${z}_{2}$-axis." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186550037 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "2c9340b5-b444-5ba2-a2cb-5082e51dd61d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186550037 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186360751 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186550038 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "2dcee10b-27d1-5c48-a0c4-bee2908f2499" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186550038 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186329693 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186550049 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "4589662c-391e-5df6-bc43-f1cd5daf48e8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186550049 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186396210 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186550060 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "5b1c82b5-04bc-5665-baac-3c0f299f6f87" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186550060 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186404651 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186550064 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "688d00e5-d04c-5be9-8532-dc349b9fa4d4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186550064 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186272162 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186550067 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "707e311b-d05c-5b00-ad03-19ab6de0f989" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186550067 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186360587 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186550072 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "8214db6b-1257-52dc-b13a-64560a045fc3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186550072 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186269075 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186550073 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "83471cd6-7315-5037-af91-304698678418" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186550073 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186419685 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186550080 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "94b498ce-dc66-55e0-84f4-0f32fbd493d6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186550080 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186550002 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186550095 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "b784e37e-64ec-5c29-9bfe-45a68c071188" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186550095 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186388167 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186550099 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "bd7824d9-adab-53ee-b13b-f281b8bd56c6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186550099 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186302305 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186550101 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "ce0cb612-f679-56f4-9fa1-b86f6c07f31c" #edb/ref 1759